## ✅ Copilot Testing

### Basic Functionality
- [ ] Ask Copilot: "How do I create a new UI test?" - Check if response references instructions
- [ ] Ask Copilot: "What's the correct way to add page locators?" - Verify mentions locators.ts
- [ ] Ask Copilot: "Should I use page.$()?" - Confirm recommends page.locator() instead
- [ ] Ask Copilot: "How do I create an API test?" - Check if mentions apiClient fixture

### Code Generation
- [ ] Request: "Create a step definition for DELETE request" - Verify follows TypeScript standards
- [ ] Request: "Generate feature file for login" - Check uses Gherkin format and tags
- [ ] Request: "Add locators for dashboard page" - Verify adds to locators.ts correctly
- [ ] Request: "Create JSON payload for user creation" - Check saves to fixtures/json/

### Pattern Recognition
- [ ] Provide hardcoded URL - Copilot should suggest ConfigUtil.getUrl()
- [ ] Provide `page.$()` - Copilot should suggest `page.locator()`
- [ ] Provide API test without status validation - Copilot should suggest adding status check
- [ ] Provide feature without tags - Copilot should suggest appropriate tags

### Agent Functionality (if using Copilot Coding Agent)
- [ ] Invoke `@test-scenario-writer` - Verify creates Gherkin scenarios
- [ ] Invoke `@locator-manager` - Verify adds to locators.ts
- [ ] Invoke `@api-test-engineer` - Verify creates API tests with proper validation
- [ ] Invoke `@step-definition-developer` - Verify creates TypeScript steps

